.TH SDL_DECLSPEC 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_DECLSPEC \- A macro to tag a symbol as a public API.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_begin_code.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_DECLSPEC __attribute__ ((visibility(\(dqdefault\(dq)))
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
SDL uses this macro for all its public functions\[char46] On some targets, it is used to signal to the compiler that this function needs to be exported from a shared library, but it might have other side effects\[char46]
.PP
This symbol is used in SDL\(aqs headers, but apps and other libraries are welcome to use it for their own interfaces as well\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

